{"overview":"Initial consonant mutation is a core feature of Welsh. The first sound of a word changes in specific grammatical environments. Soft mutation is by far the most common.","types":[{"id":"soft","welsh":"treiglad meddal","description":"Unvoiced stops become voiced; voiced stops become fricatives or disappear; ll>l, rh>r, m>f.","map":{"p":"b","t":"d","c":"g","b":"f","d":"dd","g":"","m":"f","ll":"l","rh":"r"},"common_triggers":["after i (to)","after o (from)","after am (about/for)","after dy (your, informal)","after ei (his)","feminine singular noun after y/yr/'r (the)","adjective after a feminine noun","object after a conjugated verb (SM of the object)","after dau / dwy (two)"],"examples":[{"base":"Cymru","mutated":"Gymru","context":"Croeso i Gymru — Welcome to Wales"},{"base":"tŷ","mutated":"dŷ","context":"ei dŷ — his house"},{"base":"cath","mutated":"gath","context":"y gath — the cat (fem.)"},{"base":"gardd","mutated":"ardd","context":"yr ardd — the garden"}]},{"id":"nasal","welsh":"treiglad trwynol","description":"Stops become homorganic nasals. Common after fy (my) and yn (in) in many environments.","map":{"p":"mh","t":"nh","c":"ngh","b":"m","d":"n","g":"ng"},"common_triggers":["after fy (my)","after yn meaning 'in' before many place/nouns"],"examples":[{"base":"tad","mutated":"nhad","context":"fy nhad — my father"},{"base":"pen","mutated":"mhen","context":"fy mhen — my head"},{"base":"Caerdydd","mutated":"Nghaerdydd","context":"yng Nghaerdydd — in Cardiff"}]},{"id":"aspirate","welsh":"treiglad llaes","description":"Only p, t, c become ph, th, ch. Triggered by a (and), â/gyda (with), tri (three, masc.), ei (her), and some others.","map":{"p":"ph","t":"th","c":"ch"},"common_triggers":["after a meaning 'and'","after â / gyda (with)","after ei meaning 'her'","after tri (three, masculine)"],"examples":[{"base":"tad","mutated":"thad","context":"a thad — and a father"},{"base":"ci","mutated":"chi","context":"ei chi — her dog"},{"base":"pen","mutated":"phen","context":"â phen — with a head"}]}],"possessives_quick_ref":[{"form":"fy + NM","meaning":"my","example":"fy nhad"},{"form":"dy + SM","meaning":"your (informal)","example":"dy dad"},{"form":"ei + SM","meaning":"his","example":"ei dad"},{"form":"ei + AM + h-prosthesis on vowels","meaning":"her","example":"ei thad / ei henw"},{"form":"ein + h- on vowels","meaning":"our","example":"ein tad / ein hiaith"},{"form":"eich (no mutation)","meaning":"your (formal/pl)","example":"eich tad"},{"form":"eu + h- on vowels","meaning":"their","example":"eu tad / eu hiaith"}]}